==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Only One Rarity}}

==Battleground==
*1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*2 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 166.67~170 seconds<sup>5,000f~5,100f</sup>.
*8 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*14 [[Pigeon de Sable]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*3 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage seems very threatening at first glance, but is actually rather simple to take care of. The best way to deal with the first Metal One Horn is to lure it near your base due to the very low Cat Limit. The real threats of this stage are the Li'l Bun Buns, who have exceptionally high health and DPS, and can tear through what little defense you might have.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
===='''Normal Cats'''====
*[[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] - Fast speed and fast attacks makes him a decent pick for clearing out Croconators. He can also serve as an emergency meatshield against Li'l Bun Buns. He's only decent at best, but there's no reason not to bring at least one Normal Cat.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] - ''When at higher levels'', Jamiera actually has the stats to serve as a decent tank, aside from their above-average recharge time. Their knockback can also help regain ground against The Face. As a Normal Cat, they also won't block the use of most other units.

===='''Special Cats'''====
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] - Its' knockback ability can actually see some use for once, as it can potentially knock Metal One Horn away if he gets to close to the Cat Base or a valuable unit, or can help regain some ground while dealing chip damage to The Face.

===='''Rare Cats'''====
*[[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] - Has surprisingly high stats against Floating enemies at Lv.50, with '''155,250 health''', 6,804 damage and 5,517 DPS. He can clear out Pigeon de Sables with ease, while also tanking Li'l Bun Bun and The Face. Plus, he's a Rare Cat, meaning he won't block Fishman or other Super Rares.

===='''Super Rare Cats'''====
*[[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]] - With a 100% chance for a Critical Hit and a quick foreswing, she's essentially the only unit that can guarantee an easy kill on the Metal One Horn every time. Beware that her somewhat long range might cause her to stick around for a while, so intentionally reverting her to her Normal Form for reduced health may be a good idea.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Deals massive damage against Floating enemies in a stage where most of the threats are Floating enemies. He's great for chipping away at The Face's ridiculous health pool.

